      "content": "that cannibalistic idea is pretty intense, but i want to make sure they feel truly \"other\" compared to my protagonists. i don't want them to just be \"evil\" people, i want their whole essence to feel different—like they're just fundamentally less evolved or more savage. can u go deeper into their physical appearance and how they carry themselves? like, how can i describe their look and their traditions to make them seem more wild, unrefined, and maybe a bit more primitive/tribal to really hit that contrast with the enlightened empire?",
